# Everything here is consumed by Linux tooling and containers, so the checkout
# must stay LF even when core.autocrlf=true (a common Windows/WSL default).
# CRLF breaks shebangs (`/bin/bash\r`: No such file or directory) and silently
# poisons values parsed out of text files (a go.mod version read as `v0.4.3\r`
# compares unequal to `v0.4.3`, and the stray CR mangles the terminal output).
* text=auto eol=lf
